message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite the current technical preprint using the metadata below."
title: "Computational Time Machine (CTM): A Measurement and Experimental Framework for Generational AI R&D Systems"
type: article
version: "2.0"
date-released: 2026-09-10
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22689836"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22689836"
authors:
  - given-names: "Nickolay"
    family-names: "Gorlanov"
abstract: >-
  A measurement and experimental framework for testing whether persistent,
  generational AI research systems can accelerate validated technological R&D
  progress beyond conventional parallel-agent baselines. The framework centers
  on Civilization-in-the-Loop (CitL), formalizes the Technological Time
  Compression Ratio (TTCR), introduces Causal Inheritance Depth (CID), and
  specifies controlled baselines, ablations, provenance, physical validation,
  compute and energy accounting, safety gates, and falsification criteria.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - automated AI researcher
  - generational AI R&D
  - recursive self-improvement
  - agentic research
  - Civilization-in-the-Loop
  - technological time compression
  - TTCR
  - Causal Inheritance Depth
  - CID
  - scientific discovery
  - research automation
